From 5db387767ebed0a130a4f98c1638a84436745fe3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Destrudos6 <3411622425@qq.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 15:18:37 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Add word book batch selection, move the Maimemo key, fix the
 notepad placeholder

Three rounds of user feedback on the word book:

Batch operations were missing entirely: long-pressing a card now
enters a multi-select mode (tap to toggle, select all, delete the
selection with confirmation, or sync exactly the selection), and the
selection bar replaces the normal bar while it is active.

The Maimemo open API key moved from the learning center page into
the word book itself: a "Maimemo open API" entry sits at the top of
the book. Tapping it opens the key dialog only while no key is set;
long-pressing always does, so a working key cannot be bumped by an
accidental tap. The entry lights up green once a key is stored and
verified. (The key keeps living in the default shared preferences,
so exports and cloud backups carry it along unchanged.)

The synced checkmark now lights up green (was a dark gray on-off) at
the user's request.

And the mystery of the two extra words in the Maimemo notepad is
solved and fixed: the first version created the notepad with the
placeholder line "bi pipe" (an empty content is rejected by the
API), and Maimemo's parser happily read it as the two words "Bi"
and "pipe". The test account's notepad was cleaned up live, and the
notepad is now created with the first real word lines instead - it
never needs a placeholder again. Synchronizations additionally strip
any legacy placeholder line they encounter, so notepads written by
the earlier build clean themselves out on the next sync.
